    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "Report a parse error for the first start tag inside SVG and MathML title, style, script, and noscript, for SVG and MathML textarea, xmp, iframe, noembed, noframes, and plaintext start tags, for the element's end tag inside a comment, processing instruction, or CDATA section in one of those four elements, for end tags, comments, and processing instructions in a fragment parsed into one, and for elements, and comments and processing instructions containing \"</\", that content patching or redirects insert into one. Also make the content models of the SVG title, style, and script elements in HTML documents text, and say in the syntax section that these four elements can't have element children. Parsing doesn't change: this lets conformance checkers report content that a planned parser change would parse differently.\n\nTests: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65521.\n\nPart of #11397.\n\n- [ ] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * …\n   * …\n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/65521 (the trees are today's; the tests check the `#errors` counts for non-browser parsers and conformance checkers)\n- [ ] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chromium: n/a\n   * Gecko: n/a\n   * WebKit: n/a\n   * Conformance checkers: …\n- [ ] Corresponding [HTML AAM](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/) & [ARIA in HTML](https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/) issues & PRs: n/a\n- [ ] [MDN issue](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) is filed: n/a\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a [clear commit message](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/COMMITTING.md) to use.\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n---\n\nThis is step 1 of the plan in [#11397 (comment)](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11397#issuecomment-7017950358): add parse errors where parsing would change, so conformance checkers can report such content before browsers change. The parsing change itself is #13300 (step 2). Both edit the same text, so whichever lands second needs a rebase. When #13300 lands, most of the parse errors here become dead and should be removed (the dispatcher paragraphs, the comment and processing instruction checks, and the CDATA error).\n\nNotes:\n\n- The new parse errors fire exactly where the step 2 parse differs. I checked this with a patched html5lib that implements both versions: over 460k generated and existing test inputs in 11 contexts, every input whose parse changes has a parse error. Some of those come from existing errors (such as end of file inside a tag). The harness doesn't model content patching, so the errors for that come from reading the spec text.\n- `end-tag-in-comment-cdata-or-processing-instruction` is checked in the tokenizer, where step 2 would end the element, so it doesn't fire for `<!--</title-->`. For CDATA sections it also fires in fragment parsing, where the step 2 tree doesn't change. That is intentional, so tooling can reject such input.\n- Some constructs get a new error on top of an existing one (e.g. the breakout error in `<svg><style><b>`), or two new ones for two separate future changes (`<svg><style><textarea>`).\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13301/embedded-content-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 3:06 PM UTC (70b5eac)\">/embedded-content-other.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13301/3941bb4...70b5eac/embedded-content-other.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 3:06 PM UTC (70b5eac)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13301/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 3:06 PM UTC (70b5eac)\">/infrastructure.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13301/3941bb4...70b5eac/infrastructure.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 3:06 PM UTC (70b5eac)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13301/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 3:06 PM UTC (70b5eac)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13301/3941bb4...70b5eac/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 3:06 PM UTC (70b5eac)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13301/syntax.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 3:06 PM UTC (70b5eac)\">/syntax.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13301/3941bb4...70b5eac/syntax.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2026, 3:06 PM UTC (70b5eac)\">diff</a> )",
